{
  "id": 19,
  "name": "regret_anchor_cluster",
  "intent": "Anchor on nearest-neighbor distance to preserve uniform robustness; raise regret weight relative to parent to better capture 'unique-best' candidates that pure greedy misses; lower return_distance weight to reduce early-shape bias; add tiny cluster_density pull to softly favor unvisited-dense regions on clustered instances without disturbing grid/uniform baselines.",
